(2173, 'carlo celso', '2023-11-28', '04:49:45pm', ' Today, I successfully transformed the manual process of generating reports and handling payments into an automated printing system, encompassing the reprinting of receipts, sales reports, day-end reports, Z readings, X readings, and the payment process. Additionally, I tested the automatic print with the use of thermal print to guarantee the precise alignment and polished appearance of the automatically generated receipts. Furthermore, I ensured hiding the manual printing procedures or displaying to web for all reports and the payment process.'),
(2174, 'crisjohn sunga', '2023-11-28', '04:51:29pm', ' \r\nIntroduced a new feature allowing users to provide discounts during the creation of purchase orders. If the initial discount is set to zero, users can input a discount during the purchase order list update; however, if a discount is already present, the initially inputted value takes precedence. Enhanced the receive item functionality by enabling users to edit the Cost field for both decreases and increases, with a notification system alerting users to cost changes. Any alterations in cost are reflected in the original product price.\r\n\r\nImplemented a Free Deal feature in receive items, updating the product section to dynamically reflect quantity changes. Introduced a \"Print Receive Purchase Order\" button, accessible only after item reception. Clicking this button displays item details, including Item Name, Unit, Barcode, Date Expiry, Cost, Qty, Free Deal, Discount, Total, Total Qty, and Total Cost (with an automatic deduction of discount).\r\n\r\nIn the Batch Transfer Form, users can tr'),
(2175, 'VINCENT FLORES', '2023-11-29', '09:07:10am', ' Check the displayed order if still group by name\r\n-Check the order quantity that is displayed on the kitchen printout, order-taker display, cashier, and kitchen display if its dispalying the correct value. \r\n-Check if the remarks remain attached to the item while printing to the kitchen, test adding the item with a remark and printing it to the kitchen. Then, add the item with a remark once again.\r\n-Verify if the items are grouped by name on the printed receipt and billout form.\r\n-Test the split payment feature and the receipts computation.\r\n-Check to see if the day-end report and each sales report accurately calculate the split payment.\r\n-Check the login form to see if the ordertakers credentials work with the cashier and vice versa.\r\n-Use the ordertakers new account management to review the entire process and look for any conflicts with other features or processes.\r\n-Check the reprinted receipt to make sure the calculations are accurate and the ordered item is displayed.\r\n-Check tha'),
(2176, 'VINCENT FLORES', '2023-11-28', '09:07:53am', ' Check the displayed order if still group by name\r\n-Check the order quantity that is displayed on the kitchen printout, order-taker display, cashier, and kitchen display if its dispalying the correct value. \r\n-Check if the remarks remain attached to the item while printing to the kitchen, test adding the item with a remark and printing it to the kitchen. Then, add the item with a remark once again.\r\n-Verify if the items are grouped by name on the printed receipt and billout form.\r\n-Test the split payment feature and the receipts computation.\r\n-Check to see if the day-end report and each sales report accurately calculate the split payment.\r\n-Check the login form to see if the ordertakers credentials work with the cashier and vice versa.\r\n-Use the ordertakers new account management to review the entire process and look for any conflicts with other features or processes.\r\n-Check the reprinted receipt to make sure the calculations are accurate and the ordered item is displayed.\r\n-Check tha'),
