(2223, 'carlo celso', '2023-12-11', '05:46:20pm', 'Today, I implemented the following enhancements:\r\n\r\n- Applied a per-item discount for seniors and persons with disabilities.\r\n- Configured a per-item percentage discount of 2/3 percent.\r\n- Rectified the addition of items to account for 4G Cap by product name, except when the barcode method is employed by the order taker or cashier.\r\n- Addressed quantity-related issues, ensuring that the quantity remains unchanged when using the up and down arrow buttons.\r\n- Introduced remarks for cash pullouts and incorporated them into the day-end report.\r\n- Modified the PLU search functionality to be equal rather than using the LIKE operator in SQL queries.\r\n- Resolved issues related to the application of discounts on all items.\r\n- Included a P.A (Personal Assistant) note on the receipt.\r\n- Implemented front-end reporting, encompassing all discount and special reports while considering the option to exclude SC/PWD.\r\n- Extended support for multiple branches when adding new products.\r\n- Fixed discrepan'),
(2224, 'VINCENT FLORES', '2023-12-11', '05:50:25pm', 'manually input sales to match the SI number and tally the subtotal, lessvat, pricenetvat, and amountdue of terminals 11 and 12 from the month of February to September.'),
(2225, 'ivan nunag', '2023-12-11', '05:52:10pm', '- POSTING\r\n- FOLLOW UP\r\n- SET VISIT FOR TOMORROW\r\n- MANUALLY INPUT SALES TO MATCH THE SI NUMBER AND TALLY THE SUBTOTAL, LESSVAT, PRICENETVAT, AND AMOUNT DUE OF TERMINAL 3 AND 7 FROM FEBRUARY TO SEPTEMBER.'),
(2226, 'crisjohn sunga', '2023-12-11', '06:02:45pm', ' Implemented a Purchase Order (P.O) feature, where upon receiving the P.O, the total items (pcs) are calculated and added to the products. The formula used is $totalqtypcs = ($received + $free_deal) * $totqtyunit.\r\n\r\nAdded a \"received\" status in the bucket_saveopitem table to indicate when a user has confirmed the receipt of a P.O.\r\n\r\nIntroduced a new PHP file in the sales report section named \"Purchase Order Transaction Report.\" This report provides a transaction overview within a specified date range for all suppliers. Users can click on a specific supplier to print a report tailored to that supplier. The report includes details such as Sales Invoice, Supplier, Sub Supplier, Cheque, Bank, Date, Deduction, Amount Paid, Total Amount, and Status.\r\n\r\nCreated another PHP file in the sales report section titled \"Purchase Order Delivery Report.\" This report displays pending and received delivery information for purchase orders within a specified time range. It includes details such as Lot N'),
(2227, 'VINCENT FLORES', '2023-12-12', '06:03:24pm', 'manually inputting sales data in Johnnys Supermarket Terminals 3, 11, and 12.'),
(2228, 'crisjohn sunga', '2023-12-12', '06:06:33pm', 'Doing the task for terminal 4 in janice. Finish from frb to june tomorrow will be the continuation for the remaining months '),
