(3673, 'OJT ARLFRAN', '2025-05-03', '04:22:41pm', ' DAY END REPORT\r\nMAY 03 2025\r\n\r\nAFTER BEING OUT OF THE OFFICE FOR A FEW DAYS I RESUMED WORK ON THE LAST LAYOUT I WAS EDITING AND FINALLY FINALIZED IT INCLUDING ALL NECESSARY DETAILS TO PREPARE IT FOR POSTING\r\n\r\nREACTED TO SIR RABBIâ€™S PREVIOUS POSTS AND SHARED BIRTHDAY CELEBRATION VIDEO ACROSS DIFFERENT FACEBOOK REELS GROUPS REACHING AROUND 70+ SHARES BEFORE HITTING THE DAILY LIMIT\r\n\r\nPOSTED THE NEWLY FINALIZED LAYOUT AND SHARED IT IN VARIOUS POS AND BUY AND SELL GROUPS ON FACEBOOK REACHING AROUND 40 SHARES BEFORE BEING LIMIT\r\n\r\nWENT TO MADAPDAP FOR MONTHLY MAINTENANCE AT BUDDYâ€™S MART AND BAKELKEL STARTED WITH BACKING UP FILES THEN USED THE ELECTRIC BLOWER TO CLEAN HEAVY DUST BUILDUP RETURNED IT AFTER USE THEN CHECKED PRINTER FUNCTIONALITY CLEARED PREFETCH AND TEMP FILES AND FINALLY PERFORMED A SERVER PING TEST'),
(3674, 'OJT ARLFRAN', '2025-05-05', '04:23:13pm', ' DAY END REPORT\r\nMAY 05 2025\r\n\r\nAFTER SIR RABBI LEFT I SWEPT THE ENTIRE OFFICE WHILE LARWIN PREPARED THE MOP TO CLEAN THE FLOOR RIGHT AFTER\r\n\r\nUSED LARWINâ€™S TRICYCLE TO GO TO BPI ANGELES TO DEPOSIT THE PAYMENT SLIPS\r\n\r\nSHARED MY POSTS ABOUT OUR POS PACKAGES IN DIFFERENT POS GROUPS AND BUY AND SELL GROUPS WHILE ALSO LOOKING FOR POTENTIAL CLIENTS BUT LEADS WERE SLOW AND NO ACTIVE INQUIRIES WERE RECEIVED\r\n\r\nACCOMPANIED SIR EDGAR USING LARWINâ€™S TRICYCLE TO DELIVER THE BARRIER SYSTEM TO CUTUD 3 BIGBOYS'),
(3675, 'ivan nunag', '2025-05-06', '04:31:50pm', 'DAY END REPORT 5/6/25\r\n\r\n- CREATED A NEW POSTER/ADVERTISEMENT DESIGN FOR POSTING ON THE RNZ PAGE ACCOUNT.\r\n\r\n- PREPARED A PROPER QUOTATION WITH PRICING AND PACKAGE DETAILS FOR THE ANTIQUE CLIENT.\r\n\r\n- TRANSFERRED THE FINAL EDITED RNZ COMPANY PROFILE VIDEO TO lhan.margie1999@gmail.com.\r\n\r\n- REPLIED TO CLIENT INQUIRIES AND PROVIDED ASSISTANCE THROUGH RNZ PAGE MESSENGER.\r\n\r\n- RESPONDED TO CLIENT CALLS AND ADDRESSED QUESTIONS ABOUT OUR POS SOLUTIONS.\r\n\r\n- INPUTTED EMPLOYEE ODO RECORDS ACCURATELY INTO THE SYSTEM.\r\n\r\n- POSTED AN RNZ ADVERTISEMENT TO MULTIPLE POS-RELATED FACEBOOK GROUPS.\r\n\r\n- MONITORED STAFF ATTENDANCE BY ENSURING PROPER ID TAPPING AND SYSTEM LOGIN.'),
(3676, 'Lance Garcia', '2025-05-06', '04:31:57pm', '-Technical Support Report\r\n\r\nClient Concern:\r\nThe client requested technical support due to their cashier POS kiosk system not opening.\r\n\r\nFindings:\r\nUpon inspection it was discovered that the system unit was infected with a Trojan virus which originated from their old hard disk drive. This infection prevented system applications from launching and caused the system unit to malfunction.\r\n\r\nAction Taken\r\n\r\nContacted the client and guided them through the process of resetting the system unit.\r\n\r\nAfter the reset remote access to the POS system was established using UltraViewer.\r\n\r\nInstalled the necessary RNZ installers on the POS.\r\n\r\nCopied and pasted the required system files.\r\n\r\nRendered and restored the clients data in SQL.\r\n\r\nConducted a full functionality check to ensure the POS system was operating correctly.\r\n\r\nStatus\r\nIssue resolved. The POS system is now fully operational.\r\n\r\n-Technical Support Report\r\n\r\nClient Request:\r\nThe client requested support to update their product listin'),
