(2477, '97777579', '2025-07-03', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'PORAC', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client ask for support to update their price in Best Price', 'The pricing requires an update', 'To update the price in Best Price access Best Price computer updated price and then backup their product data get the product data and execute in Best price server', 'Done'),
(2478, '39536570', '2025-07-03', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'BAKELKEL MADAPDAP', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'CLIENT REQUESTED SUPPORT TO UPDATE THEIR PRODUCT DATABASE, TRANSFERRING PRODUCT DATA FROM BUDDYâ€™S MART SERVER TO BAKELKEL AND ALSO IN BEST PRICE', 'OUTDATED PRODUCT LISTINGS ON THE BAKELKEL AND BEST PRICE', 'TO UPDATE THE PRICE FOR BAKEKEL AND BP ACCESS BUDDIES AND BP SERVER THEN BACKUP THEIR PRODUCT DATA, GET THE PRODUCT DATA AND EXECUTE IN BAKELKEL AND BEST PRICE', 'DONE'),
(2479, '22085394', '2025-07-02', 'ROSALIE  M. CABRERA', 'MAIMPIS SAN FERNANDO', 'DUKE ESGUERRA', 'CLIENT REPORTED THAT WHENEVER SHE ENTERS HER BADGE NUMBER ON THE CASHIER TERMINAL, THE SYSTEM DISPLAYS â€œINCORRECT BADGE NUMBER.â€', 'THE IP ADDRESS OF THE CASHIER UNIT HAD CHANGED, DESPITE BEING SET TO STATIC. THIS CAUSED A COMMUNICATION ISSUE BETWEEN THE POS SYSTEM AND THE SERVER, PREVENTING BADGE ID VALIDATION.', ' VIDEO CALLED THE CLIENT FOR WALKTHROUGH AND ASKED HER CHECK IF THE POS IS WIFI CONNECTED TO TP-LINK AND IT IS CONNECTED,\r\nASKED THE CLIENT TO OPEN THE COMMAND PROMPT AND ASKED HER TO TYPE IPCONFIG AND FOUND OUT THAT THE IP ADDRESS IS DIFFERENT EVEN IT IS ON STATIC.\r\nAND INSTRUCTED THE CLIENT TO SET STATIC IP ADDRESS ON THE CASHIER AND THOUGHT THE CLIENT ON HOW TO SET IT UP AFTER SETTING IT ASKED THE CLIENT TO LOGIN HER BADGE NUMBER TO CONFIRM THAT SHE CAN LOGIN TO THE CASHIER ALREADY\r\n', 'DONE'),
(2480, '93545390', '2025-07-03', 'BENNIE UY', 'BALIBAGO ANGELES CITY', 'DUKE ESGUERRA', 'CLIENT REQUESTED ASSISTANCE DUE TO A MEMORY ALLOCATION ERROR ON TERMINAL 11', 'TERMINAL 11 REQUIRED DATA EXPANSION SETTINGS TO BE ADJUSTED IN XAMPP TO RESOLVE THE MEMORY LIMIT ISSUE.', 'REQUESTED THE CLIENT TO PROVIDE ANYDESK ACCESS.\r\nACCESSED TERMINAL 11 REMOTELY AND PERFORMED DATA EXPANSION BY UPDATING THE XAMPP CONFIGURATION (E.G., PHP.INI MEMORY LIMIT).\r\nAFTER APPLYING THE CHANGES, ASKED THE CLIENT TO CONFIRM IF THE ERROR STILL PERSISTED.\r\nCLIENT CONFIRMED THAT THE ISSUE WAS RESOLVED.', 'DONE '),
(2481, '72967888', '2025-07-04', 'MARK PANGILINAN', 'SAN ISINDRO', 'Mark Tolentino', 'Scanner not working, Printer leaves a line on the receipt', 'Hardware has reached end of lifespan.', 'Contacted client to explain the issues with both the scanner and printer. Provided recommendations regarding replacement of the hardware. Advised the client to claim warranty for the printer, as it was not purchased from us.', 'DONE'),
(2482, '97777579', '2025-07-04', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'PORAC', 'DUKE ESGUERRA', 'CLIENT REQUESTED TO REPRINT THE CASHIERâ€™S DAY END REPORT AND X-READING ON TERMINAL 03 FOR THE JULY 03, 2025 REPORT.\r\n', 'CLIENT NEEDED A HARD COPY OF THE CASHIERâ€™S DAY END REPORT AND X-READING FROM YESTERDAY.\r\n', 'REQUESTED THE ANYDESK ACCESS FOR TERMINAL 03. ACCESSED THE POS SYSTEM TO BACKDATE THE CASHIER`S DAY END REPORT AND X-READING, THEN PRINTED THE REPORT. AFTER CLIENT CONFIRMATION, THE DATE AND TIME WERE SET BACK TO THE CURRENT DATE.\r\n', 'DONE'),
(2483, '53965776', '2025-07-03', 'RONALD ALLAN FRANCISCO', 'DINALUPIHAN BATAAN', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'CLIENT WANT TO ADJUST THEIR SALES FOR THE MONTH OF JUNE 2025 BOTH TERMINAL 1 AND 2', 'MONTHLY ADJUST SALES', '--ASK THE CLIENT TO OPEN THE ANYDESK OR ULTRAVIEWER TO GAIN ACCESS BOTH TERMINAL -BACK UP THE DATABASE -GET THE ITEMCOUNT.SQL AND VOIDITEMS.SQL -DELETE THE DUPLICATE OF OLD ITEMCOUNT.SQL AND VOIDITEMS.SQL -EXECUTE THE NEW ITEMCOUNT.SQL AND VOIDITEMS.SQL -SCREENSHOT THE SPECIFIC REPORT FOR THE MONTH OF MAY AND SEND IT TO SIR RAL', 'DONE'),
(2484, '53965776', '2025-07-04', 'RONALD ALLAN FRANCISCO', 'DINALUPIHAN BATAAN', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', '-Client ask for support to re adjust the sales of terminal 1 for the month of June', '-Re adjust the sale of TERMINAL 1 for the month of June 2025', '	--ASK THE CLIENT TO OPEN THE ANYDESK OR ULTRAVIEWER TO GAIN ACCESS BOTH TERMINAL -BACK UP THE DATABASE -GET THE ITEMCOUNT.SQL AND VOIDITEMS.SQL -DELETE THE DUPLICATE OF OLD ITEMCOUNT.SQL AND VOIDITEMS.SQL -EXECUTE THE NEW ITEMCOUNT.SQL AND VOIDITEMS.SQL -SCREENSHOT THE SPECIFIC REPORT FOR THE MONTH OF MAY AND SEND IT TO SIR RAL', 'Done'),
(2485, '97777579', '2025-07-04', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'PORAC', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client asked for support regarding their sales on July 3, 2025, which were save under July 2, 2025', 'The client said that they were unable to change the date on Terminal 3 on July 3, 2025, but the date shown on the computer was July 2, 2025', 'I created a backup first, then I corrected the transaction dates from July 2, 2025 to July 3, 2025.', 'Done'),
(2486, '58449021', '2025-07-04', 'MR OGIE ABESAMIS', 'TALAVERA NUEVA ECIJA', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'Client The Nest Sampaloc ask for support regarding to the adjustment sales.', 'Monthly adjustment sales', 'Back up first the databases then get the itemcount and voiditem sql and then adjust their sales regarding to their message that worth 35k and also their starting SI', 'Done'),
(2487, '15724957', '2025-07-04', 'MR OGIE ABESAMIS', 'TALAVERA NUEVA ECIJA', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'CLIENT REQUESTED AN  RE ADJUSTMENT TO THEIR SALES FOR THE MONTH OF JUNE 2025. ALTANTA MAIN', 'MONTHLY SALES ADJUSTMENT TOTALING 16163401.67 S.I. 256032 to 257477', 'ACCESS AND BACK UP DATABASE DUMP ITEMCOUNT AND VOID SQL THEN COPY TO MY COMPUTER THEN ADJUST THEIR SALES AND EXECUTE TO THEIR POS DATABASES', 'Done'),
(2488, '93545390', '2025-07-04', 'BENNIE UY', 'BALIBAGO ANGELES CITY', 'DUKE ESGUERRA', 'CLIENT REQUESTED SUPPORT FOR THE ISSUANCE DEPARTMENT. WHEN ATTEMPTING TO ENTER AN ITEM AND INPUT THE QUANTITY, THE SYSTEM DOES NOT PROCEED AND PROMPTS THE MESSAGE:\r\n\"VALUE MUST BE GREATER THAN OR EQUAL TO 1.\"', 'THE SYSTEM VALIDATION WAS STRICTLY SET TO ACCEPT ONLY WHOLE NUMBERS FOR THE QUANTITY FIELD, PREVENTING USERS FROM ENTERING FRACTIONAL VALUES (E.G., 0.5, 0.25).', 'REQUESTED THE CLIENT`S SERVER ACCESS VIA ANYDESK AND PERFORMED A BACKUP OF THE SQL DATABASE.\r\nCOORDINATED WITH THE CLIENT TO DEMONSTRATE THE EXACT PROCESS WHERE THE ISSUE OCCURRED.\r\nREVIEWED AND MODIFIED THE SYSTEM CODE TO ALLOW INPUT OF FRACTIONAL QUANTITIES (E.G., 0.5, 0.75) IN THE ISSUANCE MODULE, ENABLING SUCCESSFUL POSTING OF UNITS LESS THAN 1.\r\n', 'DONE'),
(2489, '58449021', '2025-07-04', 'MR OGIE ABESAMIS', 'TALAVERA NUEVA ECIJA', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'Client The Nest San Pascual ask for support regarding to the adjustment sales.', 'Monthly adjustment sales', 'Back up first the databases then get the itemcount and voiditem sql and then adjust their sales regarding to their message that worth 30k and also their starting SI', 'Done'),
(2490, '76279287', '2025-07-04', 'CHICKEN MALL', 'HENSON AC', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', '-Client ask for support to change their business info', '-Their business info has change to 259 GRILL', '-back up databases then update their database name and also their information regarding to business', 'Done'),
(2491, '89106584', '2025-07-04', 'SORISO RESTAURANT AND PIZERIA', 'ANGELES CITY', 'DUKE ESGUERRA', 'CLIENT REQUESTED TO IMPLEMENT A POP-UP MESSAGE DURING DAY END REPORT PROCESSING WHEN THERE ARE STILL ACTIVE TABLES WITH PENDING ORDERS. THIS IS TO PREVENT THE CASHIER FROM FORGETTING TO PROCESS OUTSTANDING PAYMENTS, ESPECIALLY SINCE THEY ARE OPERATING UNDER A SINGLE ACCOUNT\r\n', 'THE CASHIER INITIATED THE DAY END REPORT WITHOUT REALIZING THAT THERE WERE STILL UNSETTLED TABLE TRANSACTIONS, LEADING TO INCOMPLETE SALES PROCESSING.\r\n', 'ACCESSED THE CLIENTâ€™S POS SYSTEM VIA ULTRAVIEWER AND CREATED A BACKUP OF THE SQL DATABASE.\r\nMODIFIED THE INDEX.PHP FILE TO ADD A QUERY ON THE DAY END REPORT BUTTON.\r\nIMPLEMENTED A VALIDATION CHECK THAT TRIGGERS A POP-UP MESSAGE WHEN THERE ARE STILL TABLES WITH PENDING PAYMENTS.\r\nTHE SYSTEM NOW ONLY ALLOWS DAY END REPORT PROCESSING ONCE ALL TABLE TRANSACTIONS ARE FULLY CLEARED.\r\n', 'DONE'),
(2492, '62490309', '2025-07-05', 'ESTER FARIÃ‘AS', 'MORONG BATAAN', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', '-The client sent a video showing that when they click Pay Now a message appears saying \"Insufficient Stocks.', '-On some of their cashier accounts, there are transactions that were punched but not yet settled or paid', '-Accessed and backed up their database, then checked the tabpos table data. I asked them if I should clear the items that were punched in from the other cashier accounts. I also told them to try clicking Pay Now on their current transaction and then explain to them if what caused the issue and why it happened.', 'Done'),
(2493, '39536570', '2025-07-05', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'BAKELKEL MADAPDAP', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', '-Client want to update their products', '-Outdated price of products\r\n', '-To update the price for bakekel and bp access buddies and bp server then backup their product data, get the product data and execute in bakelkel and best price\r\n', 'Done'),
(2494, '97777579', '2025-07-05', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'PORAC', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', '-Client want to update their products', '-Outdated price of products', '-To update the price for bakekel and bp access buddies and bp server then backup their product data, get the product data and execute in bakelkel and best price', 'Done'),
(2495, '22085394', '2025-07-07', 'ROSALIE  M. CABRERA', 'MAIMPIS SAN FERNANDO', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', '-Deploy in SRA to answer their concerns regarding to their products and also configure the RNZ router to connect to their network lastly connect each POS and admin to UTP cable', 'We need to configure their router that is connected to their network, and we also need to connect the admin and POS via LAN cable.', 'Please advise them to avoid putting spaces at the beginning or end, as well as special characters, when inputting product names.\r\n\r\nFor the RNZ router, open a browser and enter the default IP address of the router. Then, set up the router as a range extender and connect it to their Wi-Fi or network. After that, set up the LAN cable connection and back up their databases. Finally, test if both the admin and POS are properly connected.', 'Done'),
(2496, '39557470', '2025-07-08', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'MABALACAT PAMP', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client sent a message regarding their laundry system. Their concern is that after finishing a laundry transaction, the amount shown on the POS is different from what they expect. Also their admin unit hasnt been turning on since yesterday morning.', 'For checking', 'Tomorrow morning, we will go to Cafe Beni Skytech to check what caused the issue in their system as well as in their admin system unit.', 'Pending'),
(2497, '97777579', '2025-07-08', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'PORAC', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', '-Client want to update their products', '-Outdated price of products', '-To update the price for bakekel and bp access buddies and bp server then backup their product data, get the product data and execute in bakelkel and best price', 'Done'),
(2498, '39536570', '2025-07-08', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'BAKELKEL MADAPDAP', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', '-Client want to update their products', '-Outdated price of products', '-To update the price for bakekel and bp access buddies and bp server then backup their product data, get the product data and execute in bakelkel and best price', 'Done'),
(2499, '97777579', '2025-07-08', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'PORAC', 'DUKE ESGUERRA', 'CLIENT REPORTED THAT THE CASHIER ON TERMINAL 1 COULD NOT LOG IN. THEY SAID THAT WHENEVER THEY TYPED THEIR BADGE ID IN THE LOGIN BOX, THE FIELD WAS FLICKERING, PREVENTING THEM FROM LOGGING IN.\r\n', 'POSSIBLE KEYBOARD OR MOUSE MALFUNCTION.\r\n', 'CONDUCTED VIDEO CALL WITH THE CASHIER AND REQUESTED ANYDESK ACCESS TO TERMINAL 1.\r\nCONFIRMED THE FLICKERING ISSUE DURING LOGIN ATTEMPTS.\r\nASKED THE CASHIER TO UNPLUG THE KEYBOARDXX ISSUE STILL PERSISTED.\r\nREMOTELY DISABLED THE TERMINALâ€™S KEYBOARD AND MOUSE INPUTS, THEN TESTED THE LOGIN â€” FLICKERING STOPPED.\r\nRE-ENABLED KEYBOARD AND MOUSE CONTROL.\r\nINSTRUCTED THE CASHIER TO UNPLUG THE MOUSEXX FLICKERING WAS COMPLETELY GONE DURING TESTING.\r\nCASHIER PLUGGED THE MOUSE BACK IN AND TESTED AGAIN â€', 'DONE'),
(2500, '39557470', '2025-07-09', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'MABALACAT PAMP', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client sent a message regarding their laundry system. Their concern is that after finishing a laundry transaction, the amount shown on the POS is different from what they expect. Also their admin unit hasnt been turning on since yesterday morning.', 'The client said that the power suddenly went out, so it`s possible that their admin unit experienced a power fluctuation. They also raised a concern regarding their laundry transactionsâ€”what appears on the POS printout is different from what they actually processed.', 'I performed troubleshooting on their admin computer, including RAM reseating (RAM dance), changing the SATA slot, replacing the SATA cable, resetting the CMOS, and reapplying thermal paste. I also fixed the connection between their admin unit and the POS so they can connect properly and lastly the laundry concern is for checking.', 'Done'),
(2501, '97777579', '2025-07-11', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'PORAC', 'Mark Tolentino', 'Client requested assistance in updating the product database for Best Price.', 'Outdated product listings on the Best Price system.\r\n', 'Accessed the Best Price server. Performed a backup of the existing product database. Retrieved the latest product data. Updated the product database on the Best Price system.', 'DONE'),
(2502, '10750156', '2025-07-11', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'MADAPDAP MABALACAT', 'Mark Tolentino', 'CLIENT ASKED TO UPDATE THE PRICE OF BAKELKEL AND BEST PRICE', 'Outdated product listings ', 'To update the price for bakekel and bp access buddies and bp server then backup their product data, get the product data and execute in bakelkel and best price\r\n', 'DONE'),
(2503, '39536570', '2025-07-12', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'BAKELKEL MADAPDAP', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'Client want to update their products', 'Outdated price of products', 'To update the price for bakekel and bp access buddies and bp server then backup their product data, get the product data and execute in bakelkel and best price', 'Done'),
(2504, '97777579', '2025-07-12', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'PORAC', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'Client want to update their products', 'Outdated price of products', 'To update the price for bakekel and bp access buddies and bp server then backup their product data, get the product data and execute in bakelkel and best price', 'Done'),
(2505, '39557470', '2025-07-12', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'MABALACAT PAMP', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client raised a concern because when they performed the X-reading, it showed an unusually large discount amount.', 'After reviewing the extracted database from their POS, the cashier was supposed to apply a â‚±15 discount to an item. However, what possibly happened was that when the cashier tapped the access code, possible the cursor was still on the special amount discount field, which caused the system to register a huge discount. After that, the cashier voided the item and re-added the same item to correct the discount.\r\n', 'I reviewed and checked their data, then verified the correct amount for the discount. I accessed their POS, created a backup, and updated the correct discount amount. After that, I checked their reports to ensure everything was accurate.', 'Done'),
(2506, '22085394', '2025-07-14', 'ROSALIE  M. CABRERA', 'MAIMPIS SAN FERNANDO', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client called and raised a concern regarding their printer, as it keeps printing non-stop.', 'Based on what the client said, there was no thermal paper the other day, the possible reason that all the receipts that were supposed to be printed were queued. So when they inserted the thermal paper, all of them started printing.', 'I called the client to assist them in connecting the POS to the internet so I could access it. Then, I deleted the queued print jobs from the printer. I also updated their admin server regarding the feature for adding supplies using a barcode.', 'Done'),
(2507, '44362412', '2025-07-14', 'FRIENDSHIP GARDEN RESTAURANT', 'ENCLAVE FRIENDSHIP HIWAY', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client asked for support regarding their POS storage, as it is already full', 'The storage of their POS is already full.', 'I informed the client that they need an extra storage device to transfer some of their data. Then I went to their restaurant, backed up the data first, and proceeded to delete and transfer some files.\r\n', 'Done'),
(2508, '2060918', '2025-07-14', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'MAGALANG PAMP', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client sent a message regarding their laundry system. Their concern is that after finishing a laundry transaction, the amount shown on the POS is different from what they expect.', 'Raised a concern regarding their laundry transactions—what appears on the POS printout is different from what they actually processed.', 'Access and back up their POS system and database and also copy and replace the new update for their system about to their laundry', 'Done'),
(2509, '93545390', '2025-07-14', 'BENNIE UY', 'BALIBAGO ANGELES CITY', 'DUKE ESGUERRA', 'THE CLIENT REPORTED AN ISSUE WITH THE ISSUANCE RECORDS. SPECIFICALLY, THEY OBSERVED THAT THE \"RECEIVED\" QUANTITY WAS ADDED EVEN THOUGH THERE WAS ONLY A SINGLE TRANSACTION. ADDITIONALLY, THEIR NAME APPEARS AS THE RECIPIENT IN THE SYSTEM, DESPITE NOT BEING THE ONE WHO ACTUALLY RECEIVED THE ITEMS.\r\n', 'THE ISSUE WAS POSSIBLY CAUSED BY UNPOSTING AND REPOSTING THE ISSUANCE TRANSACTION.\r\n', 'CLIENT REQUESTED AN ON-SITE VISIT TO CHECK THEIR SYSTEM. A BACKUP OF THE SQL DATABASE WAS CREATED FROM THE SERVER. AFTER BACKUP, THE CLIENT DEMONSTRATED THEIR PROCESS. THE DATABASE WAS THEN REVIEWED, AND THE CLIENT WAS ASKED HOW THEY WOULD LIKE TO RECTIFY THE ISSUE. THEY REQUESTED TO REMOVE THE AFFECTED TRANSACTION IN THE STOCKLEDGER TO CORRECT THE INVENTORY. AFTER DELETING THE TRANSACTION, THE CLIENT WAS ASKED TO VERIFY THE CORRECTION. THEY CONFIRMED THAT THE ISSUE WAS RESOLVED AND HAD NO FURTH', 'DONE'),
(2510, '39536570', '2025-07-15', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'BAKELKEL MADAPDAP', 'DUKE ESGUERRA', 'CLIENT REQUESTED SUPPORT TO UPDATE THEIR PRODUCT DATABASE, TRANSFERRING PRODUCT DATA FROM BUDDYâ€™S MART SERVER TO BAKELKEL AND ALSO IN BEST PRICE', 'OUTDATED PRODUCT LISTINGS ON THE BAKELKEL AND BEST PRICE', 'TO UPDATE THE PRICE FOR BAKEKEL AND BP ACCESS BUDDIES AND BP SERVER THEN BACKUP THEIR PRODUCT DATA, GET THE PRODUCT DATA AND EXECUTE IN BAKELKEL AND BEST PRICE', 'DONE'),
(2511, '97777579', '2025-07-15', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'PORAC', 'DUKE ESGUERRA', 'CLIENT REQUESTED SUPPORT TO UPDATE THEIR PRODUCT DATABASE, TRANSFERRING PRODUCT DATA FROM BUDDYâ€™S MART SERVER TO BAKELKEL AND ALSO IN BEST PRICE', 'OUTDATED PRODUCT LISTINGS ON THE BAKELKEL AND BEST PRICE', 'TO UPDATE THE PRICE FOR BAKEKEL AND BP ACCESS BUDDIES AND BP SERVER THEN BACKUP THEIR PRODUCT DATA, GET THE PRODUCT DATA AND EXECUTE IN BAKELKEL AND BEST PRICE', 'DONE'),
(2512, '89106584', '2025-07-15', 'SORISO RESTAURANT AND PIZERIA', 'ANGELES CITY', 'DUKE ESGUERRA', 'CLIENT REPORTED THAT WHEN PROCESSING A PAYMENT FOR A SPECIFIC TABLE, A DISCOUNT WAS BEING APPLIED EVEN THOUGH NO DISCOUNT WAS ENTERED. THEY ALSO REQUESTED AN OPTION TO INPUT QUANTITY WHEN TRANSFERRING ITEMS BETWEEN TABLES.\r\n', 'THE DISCOUNT LOGIC WAS BASED ONLY ON THE TABLE NAME, CAUSING PREVIOUSLY APPLIED DISCOUNTS TO AFFECT NEW TRANSACTIONS ON THE SAME TABLE.\r\n\r\nTHE ITEM TRANSFER FUNCTION DID NOT INCLUDE A QUANTITY SELECTION, PREVENTING PARTIAL TRANSFERS.\r\n', 'DISCOUNT PROCESSING:\r\nUPDATED THE DISCOUNT LOGIC TO INCLUDE BOTH THE TABLE NAME AND RECEIPT NUMBER. THIS ENSURES THAT DISCOUNTS APPLY ONLY TO THE INTENDED TRANSACTION AND DO NOT CARRY OVER FROM PREVIOUS SALES.\r\n\r\nITEM TRANSFER:\r\nADDED A QUANTITY INPUT TO THE TRANSFER FUNCTION. THE SYSTEM NOW ALLOWS PARTIAL TRANSFERS AND AUTOMATICALLY DEDUCTS THE TRANSFERRED QUANTITY AND AMOUNT FROM THE ORIGINAL TABLE.\r\nACCESSED THE CLIENTâ€™S SYSTEM THROUGH ULTRAVIEWER.\r\nPERFORMED A COMPLETE BACKUP OF THE SQL DA', 'DONE'),
(2513, '15724957', '2025-07-17', 'MR OGIE ABESAMIS', 'TALAVERA NUEVA ECIJA', 'Mark Tolentino', 'CLIENT NAME: BULILIT 4\r\nCLIENT ASK FOR SUPPORT REGARDING TO THEIR POS THAT THEY CAN`T REACH\r\n', 'THE XAMMP CONTROL PANEL HAS STOP', 'REMOVE THE STARTUP OF XAMMP THEN RUN AS ADMINISTRATOR OF XAMPP THEN INSTALL THE APACHE AND MYSQL THEN START BOTH\r\n\r\n', 'DONE'),
(2514, '10750156', '2025-07-17', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'MADAPDAP MABALACAT', 'Mark Tolentino', 'CLIENT ASKED TO UPDATE THE PRICE OF BAKELKEL AND BEST PRICE', 'NEED TO UPDATE PRICE', 'ACCESS BUDDYS AND BP SERVER THEN BACK UP THEIR PRODUCT DATA TO UPDATE PRICE TO BP AND BAKELKEL', 'DONE'),
(2515, '39536570', '2025-07-17', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'BAKELKEL MADAPDAP', 'Mark Tolentino', 'CLIENT ASKED TO UPDATE THE PRICE OF BAKELKEL AND BEST PRICE\r\n', 'NEED TO UPDATE PRICE', 'ACCESS BUDDYS AND BP SERVER THEN BACK UP THEIR PRODUCT DATA TO UPDATE PRICE TO BP AND BAKELKEL\r\n', 'DONE'),
(2516, '7875034', '2025-07-17', 'AIDEE GALANG HENSON', 'MADAPDAP PAMPANGA', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client sent a message saying they can`t open their admin system.', 'The POS and admin router needs to be restarted.', 'I called the client and assisted them with the necessary steps. First, I asked them to check the IP addresses of both computers to see if they had changed. Second, I performed a ping test between the two computers to check if they could communicate with each other. Lastly, I instructed them to restart their router.', 'Done'),
(2517, '52441680', '2025-07-18', 'CECILLE ROSARIO 3rd BATCH', 'URDANETA, PANGASINAN', 'DUKE ESGUERRA', 'CLIENT REPORTED THAT WHENEVER THEY PROCESS A BILL OR PAYMENT, THE ITEM QUANTITY IS NOT BEING DEDUCTED FROM THE INVENTORY, AND THERE IS NO DATA INPUT ON THE TRANSACTIONLOGS TABLE EVEN WHEN THEY INPUT A DATE.\r\n', 'UPON EXTRACTING THEIR SYSTEM FROM ONLINE AND TESTED THEIR SYSTEM LOCALLY/OFFLINE WE FOUND OUT THAT THE SYSTEM IS DEDUCTING THE PRODUCT QTY ON THE INVENTORY BECAUSE WHEN WE TESTED THE PAYMENT PROCESS ON A CERTAIN ITEM IT DEDUCT ON THE INVENTORY, AND ON THE TRANSACTION LOGS THE REASON WHY IT DOESNT SHOW ANY INPUT DUE TO DATE FORMAT.\r\n', 'WHEN WE TESTED THEIR SYSTEM ON OUR SIDE THERE IS NO PROBLEM IT DEDUCT THE QTY WAS SOLD IN THE INVENTORY AND WE TOLD THE CLIENT THAT THE ITEM SOLD IS DEDUCTING THE QTY ON THE INVENTORY, AND ON TRANSACTIONLOGS THE FORMAT OF THE DATE IS DIFFERENT WE RECTIFY THE FORMAT OF THE DATE ON POSCHECKOUTVIEW1 THAT WAS SENT TO TRANSACTIONLOGS AND NOW THEY CAN SEARCH THE DATE AND VIEW THEIR TRANSACTION LOGS PERFECTLY.\r\n', 'DONE'),
(2518, '81771722', '2025-07-18', 'MISTER BREADMAN', 'MALABANIAS', 'Charmaine Zamora', 'ðŸ“¢ IMPORTANT ANNOUNCEMENT: DOMAIN XX HOSTING RENEWAL NOTICE ðŸ“¢\r\n\r\nTo Our Valued Clients,\r\n\r\nThis is a friendly reminder that your domain and hosting services for the POS system are due for annual renewal. Since your system is hosted online, please ensure to complete the renewal on or before July 25, 2025 to avoid service interruption.\r\n\r\nðŸ”’ Failure to renew on or before the due date will result in the expiration of your domain and hosting, and your system will become temporarily inaccessib', 'ðŸ“¢ IMPORTANT ANNOUNCEMENT: DOMAIN XX HOSTING RENEWAL NOTICE ðŸ“¢\r\n\r\nTo Our Valued Clients,\r\n\r\nThis is a friendly reminder that your domain and hosting services for the POS system are due for annual renewal. Since your system is hosted online, please ensure to complete the renewal on or before July 25, 2025 to avoid service interruption.\r\n\r\nðŸ”’ Failure to renew on or before the due date will result in the expiration of your domain and hosting, and your system will become temporarily inaccessib', 'ðŸ“¢ IMPORTANT ANNOUNCEMENT: DOMAIN XX HOSTING RENEWAL NOTICE ðŸ“¢\r\n\r\nTo Our Valued Clients,\r\n\r\nThis is a friendly reminder that your domain and hosting services for the POS system are due for annual renewal. Since your system is hosted online, please ensure to complete the renewal on or before July 25, 2025 to avoid service interruption.\r\n\r\nðŸ”’ Failure to renew on or before the due date will result in the expiration of your domain and hosting, and your system will become temporarily inaccessib', 'FOR RENEWAL'),
(2519, '28522055', '2025-07-18', 'Girlie Pajarillo', 'Urdaneta City Pangasinan', 'Charmaine Zamora', 'ðŸ“¢ IMPORTANT ANNOUNCEMENT: DOMAIN XX HOSTING RENEWAL NOTICE ðŸ“¢\r\n\r\nTo Our Valued Clients,\r\n\r\nThis is a friendly reminder that your domain and hosting services for the POS system are due for annual renewal. Since your system is hosted online, please ensure to complete the renewal on or before July 25, 2025 to avoid service interruption.\r\n\r\nðŸ”’ Failure to renew on or before the due date will result in the expiration of your domain and hosting, and your system will become temporarily inaccessib', 'ðŸ“¢ IMPORTANT ANNOUNCEMENT: DOMAIN XX HOSTING RENEWAL NOTICE ðŸ“¢\r\n\r\nTo Our Valued Clients,\r\n\r\nThis is a friendly reminder that your domain and hosting services for the POS system are due for annual renewal. Since your system is hosted online, please ensure to complete the renewal on or before July 25, 2025 to avoid service interruption.\r\n\r\nðŸ”’ Failure to renew on or before the due date will result in the expiration of your domain and hosting, and your system will become temporarily inaccessib', 'ðŸ“¢ IMPORTANT ANNOUNCEMENT: DOMAIN XX HOSTING RENEWAL NOTICE ðŸ“¢\r\n\r\nTo Our Valued Clients,\r\n\r\nThis is a friendly reminder that your domain and hosting services for the POS system are due for annual renewal. Since your system is hosted online, please ensure to complete the renewal on or before July 25, 2025 to avoid service interruption.\r\n\r\nðŸ”’ Failure to renew on or before the due date will result in the expiration of your domain and hosting, and your system will become temporarily inaccessib', 'FOR RENEWAL'),
(2520, '89106584', '2025-07-19', 'SORISO RESTAURANT AND PIZERIA', 'ANGELES CITY', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client want to resize the font of amount due in their receipt', 'Re size the font of amount due', 'Access their POS and back up their databases then re size the font of amount and test then after that restore to the previous database', 'Done'),
(2521, '22085394', '2025-07-21', 'ROSALIE  M. CABRERA', 'MAIMPIS SAN FERNANDO', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client asked for support on how to view the transaction logs with each item included. They also raised concerns regarding adjusting the prices of their products, along with some other concerns.', 'The client needs to view the transactions on the terminal to monitor various reports. Additionally, their system needs to be updated so they can adjust the product prices accordingly.\r\n', 'I requested access to the server to back up and update their system. I also created a shortcut to the system so they can easily view the other transactions on the terminal. Additionally, I addressed their other concerns.', 'Done'),
(2522, '10750156', '2025-07-22', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'MADAPDAP MABALACAT', 'Mark Tolentino', 'CLIENT ASKED TO UPDATE THE PRICE OF BUDDYS AND BAKELKEL \r\n', 'NEED TO UPDATE PRICE', 'ACCESS BUDDYS SERVER THEN BACK UP THEIR PRODUCT DATA TO UPDATE PRICE IN BUDDYS AND BAKELKEL\r\n', 'DONE'),
(2523, '39536570', '2025-07-22', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'BAKELKEL MADAPDAP', 'Mark Tolentino', 'CLIENT ASKED TO UPDATE THE PRICE OF BUDDYS AND BAKELKEL', 'NEED TO UPDATE PRICE', 'ACCESS BUDDYS SERVER THEN BACK UP THEIR PRODUCT DATA TO UPDATE PRICE IN BUDDYS AND BAKELKEL', 'DONE'),
(2524, '30482321', '2025-07-22', 'Marnelli  Hipolito', 'Magalang Pamp', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client followed up regarding their concern that after performing the wash, a different value appears when the sales are rendered.', 'Update their system to remove the values that should not be included in their sales.', 'Access their POS to back up the system and data. After that, update the system, correct the previously processed wash transactions to reflect the correct values, and test the new update.', 'Done'),
(2525, '86305927', '2025-07-23', 'WOWA HARDWARES', 'EPZA', 'Mark Tolentino', 'CLIENT ASKED TO DO A MAINTENCE AND CHANGE PRINTER 58MM', 'MAINTENANCE AND INSTALL NEW 58MM PRINTER', 'PERFORMED ONSITE MAINTENANCE WITH SIR CHANU. WE COMPLETED A BACKUP OF THE POS SYSTEM, CONDUCTED GENERAL MAINTENANCE, APPLIED THERMAL PASTE, AND INSTALLED THE NEW 58MM PRINTER.', 'DONE'),
(2526, '97777579', '2025-07-23', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'PORAC', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'Client deliver their bp server pc for updating their products.', 'The client said that the device shuts down on its own or automatically, and after they had it cleaned, it stopped working completely.', 'I performed troubleshooting on its various components, and all of them were working fine except for the motherboard itself. I managed to power it on, but it only reached the BIOS screen before it automatically shut down again. I then tested a different motherboard using the working parts from the unit, and everything functioned properly. So, the issue is definitely with the motherboard.', 'Pending'),
(2527, '00000005', '2025-07-23', 'TINTIN IMPORTED CHOCOLATE SHOP', 'City of San Fernando', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', '-The client ask for support about their pos does not see the hard drive disk', '-The Operating System and other drive is set to Legacy mode so that the Operating system and other is not function properly', '-Check the BIOS to see if it detects the hard disk of the POS. -Next, change the Legacy Mode option to \"UEFI\" so that the hard disk with the operating system can be detected. Then, set the boot option 1 to the hard disk drive, save the settings, and restart. -Lastly, shut down the system and check if it proceeds to boot into the operating system.', 'Done'),
(2528, '62490309', '2025-07-24', 'ESTER FARIÃ‘AS', 'MORONG BATAAN', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', '-Client ask for support regarding in some sales and arrangement of SI on July 16-23 2025', 'Their some transaction are named it to terminal 2 and their SI number is not sequence', '-Back up databases then arrange the following sales for the july 16 2025 and arrange the SI to sequence and check if their sales and S.I then confirm to the client if its okay and done\r\n', 'Done'),
(2529, '89106584', '2025-07-24', 'SORISO RESTAURANT AND PIZERIA', 'ANGELES CITY', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'Client want to adjust the fontsize and layout for print order receipt', 'Adjust the layout and fontsize to more readable', 'Back up and get the system and database to check their concern then adjust the fontsize and layout of print order receipt then update and test to their system.', 'Done');
INSERT INTO `bucket_technotes` (`id`, `accountnum`, `xdate`, `clientname`, `address`, `techname`, `reasonoftech`, `causeoftheissue`, `resso`, `status`) VALUES
(2530, '97777579', '2025-07-25', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'PORAC', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client delivered their Best Price server PC because they said they couldnâ€™t turn it on.', 'The client said that the device shuts down on its own or automatically, and after they had it cleaned, it stopped working completely.', 'I performed troubleshooting on its various components, and all of them were working fine except for the motherboard itself. I managed to power it on, but it only reached the BIOS screen before it automatically shut down again. I then tested a different motherboard using the working parts from the unit, and everything functioned properly. So, the issue is definitely with the motherboard. I mounted the SSD on a different unit to perform a full backup. Once completed, I reformatted the drive, reins', 'Done'),
(2531, '93545390', '2025-07-25', 'BENNIE UY', 'BALIBAGO ANGELES CITY', 'DUKE ESGUERRA', 'CLIENT REPORTED THAT RECEIVING TRANSACTIONS WERE BEING DUPLICATED, RESULTING IN INCORRECT TOTAL AMOUNTS DURING THE POSTING PROCESS.\r\n', 'UPON INVESTIGATION, IT WAS CONFIRMED THAT THE ISSUE WAS CAUSED BY EITHER:\r\nSUDDEN NETWORK DISCONNECTION BETWEEN THE CLIENT TERMINAL AND THE SERVER\r\nOR\r\nACCIDENTAL PAGE RELOAD DURING THE RECEIVING PROCESS\r\n\r\nTHESE EVENTS CAUSED THE POSTTOWAREHOUSENOW.PHP SCRIPT TO RE-EXECUTE, LEADING TO MULTIPLE ENTRIES OF THE SAME TRANSACTION AND ADDITIONAL AMOUNTS BEING RECORDED.\r\n', 'ACCESSED THE SERVER USING ANYDESK WITH CLIENT`S PERMISSION.\r\n\r\nCREATED A FULL SQL DATABASE BACKUP AND SAVED A COPY OF THE EXISTING SOURCE CODE PRIOR TO MODIFICATIONS.\r\n\r\nCODE UPDATE â€“ DUPLICATE POSTING PREVENTION:\r\n\r\nMODIFIED POSTTOWAREHOUSENOW.PHP TO INCLUDE A VALIDATION CHECK.\r\n\r\nTHE SCRIPT NOW CHECKS THE STATUS FIELD IN THE BUCKET_RECEIVERLIST TABLE FOR THE SPECIFIED TRANSNUM.\r\n\r\nIF THE STATUS IS ALREADY MARKED AS \"POST TO WAREHOUSE\", THE SCRIPT STOPS EXECUTION AND DISPLAYS AN ALERT MESSAGE', 'DONE'),
(2532, '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(2533, '89106584', '2025-07-26', 'SORISO RESTAURANT AND PIZERIA', 'ANGELES CITY', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client ask for support to put time on the bill for customer and also for kitchen order and once bill payment.', 'They want to put time in each order and bill-out form helps track transactions accurately.', 'Check their concern if its possible then update the system to input time in bill out form and print order then test and access their pos and back up their system then update.', 'Done'),
(2534, '64857706', '2025-07-26', 'MS.PAULA JOY', 'STO ROSARIO TAVERA', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client ask for support about their webcam does not function in their attendance', 'The browser on their PC does not have the permission to use the camera enabled.', 'Call the client and asst them to unplug and plug the webcam then after that access their pc to check and enable the permission to use the webcam in their attendance system', 'Done'),
(2535, '10750156', '2025-07-26', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'MADAPDAP MABALACAT', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client has a concern regarding their laundry system: after selecting a date and it starts computing, the screen turns white and the process does not continue.', 'While checking some data on all terminals, some table data was found to be missing.', 'I first checked all the terminals, then I took the file system and database from one terminal and we checked it here. Also, Simon reprogrammed something in their system and test. After that, I accessed each terminal remotely, backed up the databases and system files from all terminals, then I inputted the missing tables into the databases and conducted tests.', 'Done'),
(2536, '97777579', '2025-07-28', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'PORAC', 'DUKE ESGUERRA', 'THE CLIENT REQUEST SUPPORT TO UPDATE THEIR PRODUCTS FROM THE SERVER TO BEST PRICE\r\n', 'UPDATE THEIR OUTDATED PRODUCTS\r\n', 'ACCESS THE BP SERVER AND BACKUP THE PRODUCT SQL TO UPDATE THE PRICING TO BEST PRICE ADMIN PORAC\r\n', 'DONE'),
(2537, '71583918', '2025-07-28', 'MK AMANTE', 'NARVACAN ILOCOS SUR', 'Rabbi Zamora', 'Client reached out via chat to request assistance in updating the POS system by adding a new fuel station (Station 4) and assigning six (6) new pumps (Pump 1 to Pump 6) under this station.', 'The current POS configuration did not include Station 4 and its corresponding pump assignments. This limited the client`s ability to manage and monitor operations for the newly installed pumps at Station 4.', '1. Accessed the backend of the POS system.\r\n\r\n2. Configured and integrated Station 4 into the systemâ€™s station management module.\r\n\r\n3. Created and mapped six (6) pump entries (Pump 1 to Pump 6) under Station 4, ensuring they are properly labeled and linked to the correct station ID.\r\n\r\n4. Performed system validation and testing to ensure the new station and pumps were functioning properly within the POS interface.\r\n\r\n5. Advised the client to update the fuel price list in the system before sta', 'Task successfully completed. Station 4 and Pumps 1 to 6 are now fully operational and reflected in the POS system.'),
(2538, '29023954', '2025-07-29', 'PATRICIA SIMPLE', 'CAPAS TARLAC', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'Client ask for support regarding to their negatives sales in the of July 10 2025 also delete some products because while purchasing it will stock up in white screen.', 'Wrong process in discounting and also delete some products due to input a special charaters', 'Access and back up database then update the exact discount to the wrong discount amount and delete some products.', 'Done'),
(2539, '62490309', '2025-07-29', 'ESTER FARIÃ‘AS', 'MORONG BATAAN', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'Client ask for support regarding in arrangement of SI on July 15-29 2025 and also their  date of the terminal 1 is not synced with the correct time.', 'Some date the SI number are not sequence, also their date is not syncing properly due to an old CMOS battery or USB dongle.', 'I accessed and backed up their database, then sequenced their SI number starting at 55738 after the client mentioned that their dongle was new. I then tried syncing the date and told them to monitor it first. Once everything is working fine, they can proceed to the other terminal to fix it as well.\r\n', 'Done'),
(2540, '89106584', '2025-07-30', 'SORISO RESTAURANT AND PIZERIA', 'ANGELES CITY', 'DUKE ESGUERRA', 'CLIENT REQUESTED TO INCREASE THE FONT SIZE OF ITEM NAMES, GROSS TOTAL, DISCOUNTS, AND SERVICE CHARGE ON THE PRINTED RECEIPT.\r\n', 'THEY MENTIONED THAT THE RECEIPT IS HARD TO READ AT NIGHT, ESPECIALLY FOR THEIR SENIOR CUSTOMERS.\r\n', 'CLIENT PROVIDED ULTRAVIEWER ACCESS FOR REMOTE SUPPORT.\r\n\r\nBACKED UP THE CLIENT`S SQL DATABASE.\r\n\r\nUPDATED FONT SIZES IN PRINTBILL.PHP AND POSCHECKOUTPRINTNOW1.PHP ACCORDING TO CLIENT`S REQUEST.\r\n\r\nINFORMED THE CLIENT THAT THE ADJUSTMENTS WERE MADE AND ASKED FOR CONFIRMATION IF THE CHANGES WERE ACCEPTABLE.\r\n', 'DONE'),
(2541, '39536570', '2025-07-31', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'BAKELKEL MADAPDAP', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'Client want to update their products', 'Outdated price of products', 'To update the price for bakekel access buddies mart server and then backup their product data, get the product data and execute in bakelkel.', 'Done'),
(2542, '97777579', '2025-07-31', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'PORAC', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'Client want to update their products', 'Outdated price of products', 'To update the price for bakekel access buddies mart server and then backup their product data, get the product data and execute in bakelkel.\r\n', 'Done'),
(2543, '62490309', '2025-07-31', 'ESTER FARIÃ‘AS', 'MORONG BATAAN', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client sent a photo regarding the Sales Invoices for the month of July 2025, stating that they are not in sequence.', 'Based on the data, there are instances when the terminal number of the POS changes, which causes the SI sequence to change as well.', 'Access and back up their system, then check the Sales Invoices (SI) and the system settings to fix the issue with the changing terminal number. After that, organize the SI and bucket receipt numbers in proper sequence.', 'Done'),
(2544, '15724957', '2025-08-01', 'MR OGIE ABESAMIS', 'TALAVERA NUEVA ECIJA', 'DUKE ESGUERRA', 'CLIENT REQUESTED AN RE ADJUSTMENT TO THEIR SALES FOR THE MONTH OF JULY 2025. ALTANTICPLUS', 'MONTHLY SALES ADJUSTMENT TOTALING 1,226,137.91 S.I. 15155 to 15622', 'ACCESS AND BACK UP DATABASE DUMP ITEMCOUNT AND VOID SQL THEN COPY TO MY COMPUTER THEN ADJUST THEIR SALES AND EXECUTE TO THEIR POS DATABASES', 'DONE'),
(2545, '39557470', '2025-08-02', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'MABALACAT PAMP', 'DUKE ESGUERRA', 'CLIENT REPORTED THAT CARD PAYMENTS DO NOT APPEAR WHEN PROCESSING THE DAY-END REPORT.', 'IN THE PRINTDAYEND REPORT CODE, CARD PAYMENTS WERE LABELED AS \"CCARD\" INSTEAD OF \"CARD\", CAUSING THEM NOT TO DISPLAY.', 'REQUESTED ULTRAVIEWER ACCESS FROM THE CLIENT.\r\n\r\nSAVED A BACKUP OF THE DATABASE (SQL FILE).\r\n\r\nCHECKED AND EDITED THE PRINTDAYEND REPORT CODE TO CORRECT THE LABELING.\r\n\r\nCOORDINATED WITH CLIENT FOR CONFIRMATION IF THE ISSUE WAS RESOLVED.\r\n', 'DONE'),
(2546, '89619961', '2025-08-02', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'NA', 'DUKE ESGUERRA', 'CLIENT REPORTED THAT CARD PAYMENTS DO NOT APPEAR WHEN PROCESSING THE DAY-END REPORT', 'IN THE PRINTDAYEND REPORT CODE, CARD PAYMENTS WERE LABELED AS \"CCARD\" INSTEAD OF \"CARD\", CAUSING THEM NOT TO DISPLAY.', 'REQUESTED ULTRAVIEWER ACCESS FROM THE CLIENT. SAVED A BACKUP OF THE DATABASE (SQL FILE). CHECKED AND EDITED THE PRINTDAYEND REPORT CODE TO CORRECT THE LABELING. COORDINATED WITH CLIENT FOR CONFIRMATION IF THE ISSUE WAS RESOLVED.', 'DONE'),
(2547, '2060918', '2025-08-01', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'MAGALANG PAMP', 'DUKE ESGUERRA', 'CLIENT REPORTED THAT CARD PAYMENTS DO NOT APPEAR WHEN PROCESSING THE DAY-END REPORT.', 'IN THE PRINTDAYEND REPORT CODE, CARD PAYMENTS WERE LABELED AS \"CCARD\" INSTEAD OF \"CARD\", CAUSING THEM NOT TO DISPLAY.', 'REQUESTED ULTRAVIEWER ACCESS FROM THE CLIENT. SAVED A BACKUP OF THE DATABASE (SQL FILE). CHECKED AND EDITED THE PRINTDAYEND REPORT CODE TO CORRECT THE LABELING. COORDINATED WITH CLIENT FOR CONFIRMATION IF THE ISSUE WAS RESOLVED.', 'DONE'),
