(2991, '58449021', '2026-05-09', 'MR OGIE ABESAMIS', 'TALAVERA NUEVA ECIJA', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'Client send the monthly adjustment sales for the month of April 2026', 'San pascual - Monthly sales adjustment Need sales worth 27k SI No. - 29415\r\nSampaloc - Monthly sales adjustment Need sales worth 32k SI No. - 55790 \r\n', 'Asked the client to open ultraviewer to gain access backed up the database dump itemcount.sql and voiditems.sql and adjusted the sales after that access executed the updated itemcount.sql and voiditems.sql files to their database.', 'Done'),
(2992, '88556487', '2026-05-09', 'CHARLOTTE SIBAL', 'INFINITY AC', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'Client ask for support regarding to their 2 tablets that are not connected to kitchen and motchi display ', 'The lan in the router is disconnected.', 'Call the client to assist them to replug the lan utp cable then check it the ip address of POS then set it to static then set also the link to the kitchen and mochi display.', 'Done'),
(2993, '66165111', '2026-05-13', 'MARK DY', 'CITY OF SAN FERNANDO', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client requested technical assistance due to visible horizontal lines appearing on the monitor screen, which caused concern regarding the monitorâ€™s display performance.', 'The monitor was experiencing display glitches, showing multiple horizontal lines across the lower part of the screen while the display remained visible and functional.\r\n', 'Visited the clientâ€™s store to inspect and test the monitor. After confirming the issue, the defective touchscreen monitor was replaced with a new touchscreen monitor. The old monitor was pulled out and retrieved without the original box.', 'Done'),
(2994, '93545390', '2026-05-13', 'BENNIE UY', 'BALIBAGO ANGELES CITY', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'Client send a photo regarding to their printed transaction but cant reprint the transaction', 'The service invoice transaction is missing from the database.', 'Access the client POS then backup database then input manually the data of that transactions SI no. 26422 then reprint that transaction.', 'Done'),
(2995, '88556487', '2026-05-13', 'CHARLOTTE SIBAL', 'INFINITY AC', 'JEROLD OYANDO', 'Client reported that she can`t access the admin and the sales management on her laptop', 'A new issue occurred because after replugging the LAN UTP cable, the IP address of the POS changed.', 'Accessed the POS to check its IP address, then accessed the admin side to update the old IP address with the new one.\r\n', 'DONE'),
(2996, '66165111', '2026-05-14', 'MARK DY', 'CITY OF SAN FERNANDO', 'JAMES BRYAN YABUT', 'The client requested technical assistance regarding the application freezing after processing a cash out slip transaction.', 'The application became unresponsive or frozen for approximately 10 minutes after the cash out slip was processed.', 'The client was instructed to restart the application by closing and reopening the system, then try to process another cash out slip. The application resumed normal operation afterward.', 'DONE'),
(2997, '64857706', '2026-05-18', 'MS.PAULA JOY', 'STO ROSARIO TAVERA', 'JAMES BRYAN YABUT', 'Client requested assistance in extracting the Daily Sales report for May 1 from the Daily End Report.', 'The requested Day-End Report for May 1 could no longer be generated using the current system date settings.', 'The client provided UltraViewer (UV) access to the POS system. Performed an SQL backup and saved a secure copy of the database.\r\nTemporarily changed the system date to the required reporting date to successfully generate and print the Day-End Report for Maâ€™am Jane.\r\nAfter the report was printed and confirmed by the client, the system date was restored to the current date.', 'DONE'),
(2998, '97777579', '2026-05-19', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'PORAC PAMPANGA', 'JAMES BRYAN YABUT', 'The client requested an update of product prices in both Best Price and Bakelkel systems.', 'The product prices in Best Price and Bakelkel were outdated.', 'Updated the prices for Bakelkel and Best Price using BP Access Buddies and the BP Server. \r\nBacked up the product data, retrieved the updated product information, \r\nand executed the updates in both Bakelkel and Best Price systems.', 'DONE'),
(2999, '10750156', '2026-05-19', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'MADAPDAP MABALACAT', 'JAMES BRYAN YABUT', 'The client requested an update of product prices in both Best Price and Bakelkel systems.', 'The product prices in Best Price and Bakelkel were outdated.', 'Updated the prices for Bakelkel and Best Price using BP Access Buddies and the BP Server. \r\nBacked up the product data, retrieved the updated product information, \r\nand executed the updates in both Bakelkel and Best Price systems.', 'DONE'),
(3000, '39536570', '2026-05-19', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'BAKELKEL MADAPDAP', 'JAMES BRYAN YABUT', 'The client requested an update of product prices in both Best Price and Bakelkel systems.', 'The product prices in Best Price and Bakelkel were outdated.', 'Updated the prices for Bakelkel and Best Price using BP Access Buddies and the BP Server. \r\nBacked up the product data, retrieved the updated product information, \r\nand executed the updates in both Bakelkel and Best Price systems.', 'DONE'),
(3001, '8322230', '2026-05-20', 'CENTRAL GRILL', 'ANGELES CITY', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client requested technical support because their POS system was not functioning properly, and the power was repeatedly turning on and off.', 'Due to a power outage that lasted for several days, the POS system automatically shut down unexpectedly.', 'Arrived at the clientâ€™s restaurant and performed troubleshooting and maintenance on the POS system. After successfully turning on the POS, backed up the database and file system. Tested the POS to ensure it was functioning properly, then conducted a stress test for system stability. Lastly, informed the client on the proper usage of the UPS to avoid similar issues in the future.', 'Done'),
(3002, '7648968', '2026-05-20', 'RUTH ALONZO', 'PANDAN ANGELES CITY', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client requested technical support for the installation of their new printer.', 'The existing printer was not printing properly because the printer gear was already worn out, causing issues during printing.', 'Arrived at the clientâ€™s store and performed a database backup. Replaced the old printer with a new printer, installed the necessary printer drivers, conducted a test print, and verified printer functionality through the POS system.', 'Done'),
(3003, '7648968', '2026-05-20', 'RUTH ALONZO', 'PANDAN ANGELES CITY', '', 'Receipt printer was not printing in the correct size. The printed receipt output \r\nappeared smaller than the actual paper width during cashier transactions.', 'The Google Chrome window was in a minimized or reduced display format, causing the printer \r\nsettings to not properly detect \r\nthe configured 80mm paper size and resulting in the receipt printing in a smaller default size.', 'Provided remote assistance to the client through a call. Guided the client in correctly configuring the printer \r\npaper size settings and instructed her to reopen \r\nthe Google Chrome window and adjust it to full screen, as it was previously minimized. After applying the necessary adjustments, \r\na test print was performed and the receipt printed correctly at the proper size.', 'DONE'),
(3004, '97777579', '2026-05-21', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'PORAC PAMPANGA', 'JAMES BRYAN YABUT', 'The client requested an update of product prices in both the Bakelkel and Best Price systems.', 'The product prices in both Bakelkel and Best Price systems were outdated.', 'Updated the product prices for Bakelkel and Best Price using BP Access Buddies and the BP Server. Backed up the product data, retrieved the updated product information, and successfully executed the updates in both systems.', 'DONE'),
(3005, '10750156', '2026-05-21', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'MADAPDAP MABALACAT', 'JAMES BRYAN YABUT', 'The client requested an update of product prices in both the Bakelkel and Best Price systems.', 'The product prices in both Bakelkel and Best Price systems were outdated.', 'Updated the product prices for Bakelkel and Best Price using BP Access Buddies and the BP Server. Backed up the product data, retrieved the updated product information, and successfully executed the updates in both systems.', 'DONE'),
(3006, '39536570', '2026-05-21', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'BAKELKEL MADAPDAP', 'JAMES BRYAN YABUT', 'The client requested an update of product prices in both the Bakelkel and Best Price systems.', 'The product prices in both Bakelkel and Best Price systems were outdated.', 'Updated the product prices for Bakelkel and Best Price using BP Access Buddies and the BP Server. Backed up the product data, retrieved the updated product information, and successfully executed the updates in both systems.', 'DONE'),
(3007, '330124', '2026-05-22', 'MARK DY', 'TELABASTAGAN', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client requested technical support regarding sales adjustment for May 17, 2026, because not all transactions were being adjusted successfully.', 'One transaction had no OR number and incomplete data in the table used for adjusting per item, which caused the adjustment process to fail for the remaining transactions.', 'Accessed the POS system and performed a database backup. Simulated and checked each transaction to verify if all data were complete. Found one transaction with missing data, which prevented the other transactions from being adjusted properly. Refunded the affected SI number, then instructed the client to retry the sales adjustment process. After retrying, the adjustment was completed successfully.', 'Done'),
(3008, '88556487', '2026-05-25', 'CHARLOTTE SIBAL', 'INFINITY AC', 'JAMES BRYAN YABUT', 'The client reported that the merchandise products could not be processed and printed in the POS system.', 'The category of the merchandise items was set to â€œAdd-ons,â€ which caused the merchandise products to not be processed and printed in the POS system.', 'Accessed the clientâ€™s POS computer and edited the database category of the merchandise items from â€œAdd-onsâ€ to â€œMochiâ€ so the merchandise products could be properly processed and printed in the POS system. Conducted testing afterward to verify that the merchandise items were already processing and printing successfully.', 'DONE'),
(3009, '330124', '2026-05-26', 'MARK DY', 'TELABASTAGAN', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client requested technical support regarding sales adjustment for May 22, 2026, because not all transactions were being adjusted successfully.', 'Two transaction had no OR number and incomplete data in the table used for adjusting per item, which caused the adjustment process to fail for the remaining transactions.', 'Accessed the POS system and performed a database backup. Simulated and checked each transaction to verify if all data were complete. Found two transaction with missing data, which prevented the other transactions from being adjusted properly. Lock the affected SI number, then instructed the client to retry the sales adjustment process. After retrying, the adjustment was completed successfully.', 'Done'),
(3010, '330124', '2026-05-26', 'MARK DY', 'TELABASTAGAN', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client requested technical support regarding sales adjustment for May 25, 2026, because not all transactions were being adjusted successfully.', 'One transaction had no OR number and incomplete data in the table used for adjusting per item, which caused the adjustment process to fail for the remaining transactions.', 'Accessed the POS system and performed a database backup. Checked each transaction to verify if all data were complete. Found one transaction with missing data, which prevented the other transactions from being adjusted properly. Locked the affected SI number and instructed the client to retry the sales adjustment process. After retrying, the adjustment was completed successfully.\r\n\r\nLastly, we simulated each transaction with no OR number and determined that the transactions were duplicated. I as', 'Done'),
(3011, '39536570', '2026-05-29', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'BAKELKEL MADAPDAP', 'JAMES BRYAN YABUT', 'Client asked to update the price of bakelkel.', 'outdated price of product', 'Accessed Buddyâ€™s server and performed a full SQL backup. Extracted the product data from the database, then retrieved and transferred the data for integration. Subsequently accessed the Bakelkel system and executed the product data import to ensure proper synchronization.', 'DONE'),
(3012, '28522055', '2026-05-30', 'Girlie Pajarillo', 'Urdaneta City Pangasinan', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client requested technical support regarding an exchange item transaction that was processed yesterday. The quantity of the exchanged item was entered incorrectly. It should have been 1, but 14 was mistakenly entered instead. As a result, the inventory and transaction records showed a negative variance of 2,221.', 'Human error during transaction processing caused the incorrect quantity to be entered. Instead of recording a quantity of 1, a quantity of 14 was mistakenly encoded, resulting in discrepancies in the inventory and transaction records.', 'Accessed the online database and performed a full database backup before making any changes. The system was then configured to run in a local testing environment for validation. All transactions related to the incorrect exchange item process were reviewed and verified. The affected transaction was adjusted and corrected accordingly. After completing the correction, the client was asked to verify the transaction and confirm that the sales and reports were already accurate and balanced.', 'Done'),
(3013, '16364842', '2026-06-01', 'JONALYN BENGANO', 'TAGUIG', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client requested technical support because the POS system was displaying an \"Incorrect Badge Number\" error whenever users attempted to log in.', 'According to the client, the cashier was able to log in successfully earlier in the morning. However, after a few minutes, the cashier could no longer access the POS system. The issue occurred after their router was reset, which likely caused changes in the network configuration.', 'Contacted the client to verify whether the cashier and server computers were connected to the same network router. Assisted the client in checking the IP addresses of both devices and found that the server`s IP address had changed. Configured a static IP address for the server and tested the connection from the cashier workstation. After the configuration, the cashier was able to log in successfully using the badge number.', 'Done'),
