(3020, '15724957', '2026-06-05', 'MR OGIE ABESAMIS', 'TALAVERA NUEVA ECIJA', 'JAMES BRYAN YABUT', 'Client sent the monthly sales adjustments for May 2026.\r\nAtlanta Sto. Rosario, Andal Lino, and Sibul.', 'Monthly Sales Adjustments need for the branches of:\r\nSto. Rosario - Sales adjustment of 1,142,423.87, Starting SIXX 22500.\r\nAndal Lino - Sales adjustment of 862,730.31, Starting SIXX 53701.\r\nSibul - Sales adjustment of 761,306.64, Starting SIXX 23591.', 'Asked the client to open AnyDesk to gain access for Sto. Rosario, Andal Lino, and Sibul. Performed a database backup for each location, Then dumped the itemcount.sql and voiditems.sql, Paid all transactions and adjusted the sales, and after that access, Executed the updated itemcount.sql and voiditems.sql files into their respective databases.', 'DONE'),
(3021, '39536570', '2026-06-08', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'BAKELKEL MADAPDAP', 'JAMES BRYAN YABUT', 'Client asked to update the price of bakelkel.', ' outdated price of product', 'Accessed Buddyâ€™s server and performed a full SQL backup. Extracted the product data from the database, then retrieved and transferred the data for integration. Subsequently accessed the Bakelkel system and executed the product data import to ensure proper synchronization.', 'DONE'),
(3022, '97777579', '2026-06-10', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'PORAC PAMPANGA', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client requested assistance in deleting an item that was mistakenly entered with an incorrect quantity.', 'While adding items to the transaction, an incorrect quantity was accidentally entered for one of the items.', 'Accessed the client`s POS system and created a backup of the database. Located the voided item in the database and successfully removed the incorrect transaction record.', 'Done'),
(3023, '39536570', '2026-06-10', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'BAKELKEL MADAPDAP', 'JAMES BRYAN YABUT', ' Client asked to update the price of bakelkel.', 'outdated price of product', 'Accessed Buddyâ€™s server and performed a full SQL backup. Extracted the product data from the database, then retrieved and transferred the data for integration. Subsequently accessed the Bakelkel system and executed the product data import to ensure proper synchronization.', 'DONE'),
(3024, '39536570', '2026-06-10', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'BAKELKEL MADAPDAP', 'JAMES BRYAN YABUT', 'Client reported that Terminal 4 is failing to boot properlyXX the unit receives power, but the system does not remain powered on.', 'Power instability and electrical fluctuations caused stress to the power supply unit, triggering a system-wide error state.', 'Conducted an initial troubleshooting process on-site to identify the source of the power failure, but the unit remained unresponsive. The unit was then pulled out for a detailed physical inspection at the office. Performed a full power supply unit (PSU) reset and cleared all underlying component error states. Finally, the system was stress-tested to ensure all hardware was functioning correctly and to restore stable, reliable booting functionality.\r\n', 'DONE'),
(3025, '97777579', '2026-06-12', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'PORAC PAMPANGA', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client requested support regarding a transaction wherein the receipt was successfully printed, but the items that were punched remained in the cart and were not cleared from the POS system.', 'Possible system or user-related issue wherein the cart was not cleared after the transaction settlement was completed.', 'Accessed the client`s POS system and verified that the transaction had already been successfully saved. Advised the client to manually clear the remaining items in the cart before proceeding with a new transaction. Confirmed that normal transaction processing could continue afterward.', 'Done'),
(3026, '39536570', '2026-06-12', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'BAKELKEL MADAPDAP', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'Client want to update their products in bakelkel', 'Outdated price of products of bakelkel', 'Get the updated price in buddys server then access the POS of bakelkel and render it the updated products.', 'Done'),
(3027, '39536570', '2026-06-16', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'BAKELKEL MADAPDAP', 'JAMES BRYAN YABUT', 'Client want to update their products in bakelkel', 'Outdated price of products of bakelkel', 'Get the updated price in buddys server then access the POS of bakelkel and render it the updated products.', 'Done'),
(3028, '39536570', '2026-06-19', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'BAKELKEL MADAPDAP', 'JAMES BRYAN YABUT', 'Client want to update their products in bakelkel', 'Outdated price of products of bakelkel', 'Get the updated price in buddys server then access the POS of bakelkel and render it the updated products.', 'Done'),
(3029, '94506167', '2026-06-20', 'MARLON TOLENTINO', 'CONCEPCION TARLAC', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client requested support regarding Terminal 2, which was experiencing very slow performance during login and while processing transactions. The same issue was also observed on the server.', 'The issue was possibly caused by the network configuration. The server was connected to a network setup that was affected by internet-related settings, resulting in delays in communication between the server and terminals.', 'Assisted the client in checking the IP configuration of Terminal 2 and verified the network settings. Configured the server with a proper static IP address suitable for the store`s local network environment without internet dependency. After the adjustments, the connection between the server and terminals returned to normal operation.', 'Done'),
(3030, '10750156', '2026-06-09', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'MADAPDAP MABALACAT', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'Client reported that Terminal 4 is failing to boot properlyXX the unit receives power, but the system does not remain powered on.', 'Power instability and electrical fluctuations caused stress to the power supply unit, triggering a system-wide error state.', 'Conducted an initial troubleshooting process on-site to identify the source of the power failure, but the unit remained unresponsive. The unit was then pulled out for a detailed physical inspection at the office. Performed a full power supply unit (PSU) reset and cleared all underlying component error states. Finally, the system was stress-tested to ensure all hardware was functioning correctly and to restore stable, reliable booting functionality.', 'Done'),
(3031, '10750156', '2026-06-20', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'MADAPDAP MABALACAT', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'Client requested support because Terminal 4 could not be powered on. The system unit was not turning on.', 'Possible motherboard failure due to a short circuit, preventing the system unit from powering on.', 'Performed troubleshooting on the system unit and tested each hardware component to identify the faulty part. After confirming that the motherboard was short, replaced the motherboard and conducted testing to ensure the system unit was functioning properly.', 'Done'),
(3032, '10396687', '2026-06-23', 'SKY SAUNA CORP.', 'CLARK FREEPORT ZONE PAMPANGA', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'Client requested support because they were unable to log in to the POS system. According to the cashier, the POS automatically logged out after being left idle for several minutes.', 'The issue was caused by the system`s security feature, which automatically locks or terminates the current session when the account remains inactive for an extended period.', 'Called the client and instructed them to open UltraViewer for remote assistance. Accessed the POS system and verified that there was no issue with the account. Explained to the cashier that the logout was due to the system`s inactivity security feature. Advised them that if the issue occurs again, they can press Alt XX F4 to close the login window and then click the Cashier icon to log in again.', 'Done'),
(3033, '18019772', '2026-06-24', 'ANALYN KIDKID', 'ILOGON BENGUET', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'Client requested support regarding Terminal 1 of their POS system. The CPU fan was repeatedly turning on and off, causing the POS system to fail to boot properly.\r\n', 'The motherboard of Terminal 1 was found to be defective, possibly due to a short circuit.', 'The client shipped the POS system unit to POS for troubleshooting. After extensive testing and diagnosis, the motherboard was replaced, which successfully restored the system unit`s functionality.\r\n\r\nA full backup of the POS system and database was performed. The backup data was restored and installed on the new server system unit. After installation and testing were completed, both the repaired POS system unit and the new server were shipped back to the client.\r\n\r\nCalled the client and assisted', 'Done'),
(3034, '88556487', '2026-06-27', 'CHARLOTTE SIBAL', 'INFINITY AC', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client requested onsite support because their sticker printer was producing loud noises during printing and was unable to print the complete label content.', 'Upon inspection, several internal components were found to be damaged. The printer`s gear/motor assembly was defective, causing abnormal noise during operation and preventing the printer from feeding and printing labels properly.', 'Performed an onsite inspection and confirmed that the sticker printer was defective due to damaged internal components. Replaced the faulty printer with a new unit, installed the necessary driver and configuration, restored the printer settings, and conducted print testing. The new sticker printer was functioning normally after the replacement.', 'Done'),
(3035, '15724957', '2026-07-01', 'MR OGIE ABESAMIS', 'TALAVERA NUEVA ECIJA', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'Client send the monthly adjustment sales for the month of May 2026\r\nMAESTRANG KIKAY', 'Monthly sales adjustment Need sales 979663.28SI No. - 16118', 'Asked the client to open ultraviewer to gain access backed up the database dump itemcount.sql and voiditems.sql and paid all transactions and adjusted the sales, after that access executed the updated itemcount.sql and voiditems.sql files to their database.', 'Done'),
(3036, '15724957', '2026-07-01', 'MR OGIE ABESAMIS', 'TALAVERA NUEVA ECIJA', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'Client send the monthly adjustment sales for the month of June 2026 ESGUERRA\r\n', 'Monthly sales adjustment Need sales 612209.91 SI No. - 6752', 'Asked the client to open ultraviewer to gain access backed up the database dump itemcount.sql and voiditems.sql and paid all transactions and adjusted the sales, after that access executed the updated itemcount.sql and voiditems.sql files to their database.', 'Done'),
(3037, '15724957', '2026-07-01', 'MR OGIE ABESAMIS', 'TALAVERA NUEVA ECIJA', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'Client send the monthly adjustment sales for the month of June 2026 STO DOMINGO', 'Monthly sales adjustment Need sales 2,263,478.73  SI No. - 32516\r\n', 'Asked the client to open ultraviewer to gain access backed up the database dump itemcount.sql and voiditems.sql and adjusted the sales, after that access executed the updated itemcount.sql and voiditems.sql files to their database.', 'Done'),
(3038, '15724957', '2026-07-01', 'MR OGIE ABESAMIS', 'TALAVERA NUEVA ECIJA', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'Client send the monthly adjustment sales for the month of June 2026 ATLANTICPLUS\r\n', 'Monthly sales adjustment Need sales 1,472,304.81  SI No. - 21242', 'Asked the client to open ultraviewer to gain access backed up the database dump itemcount.sql and voiditems.sql and adjusted the sales, after that access executed the updated itemcount.sql and voiditems.sql files to their database.', 'Done'),
(3039, '28522055', '2026-07-02', 'Girlie Pajarillo', 'Urdaneta City Pangasinan', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'Client ask for support for additional admin account and also accesscode for re-print receipt, discounts, voids, item Exchange.', 'Additional admin account and accesscode', 'Tell the client to send the details of the new admin account then personally message me then input and add additional account and access for admin then tell the client to test the account.', 'Done'),
(3040, '93545390', '2026-07-03', 'BENNIE UY', 'BALIBAGO ANGELES CITY', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client requested support regarding the delivery creation process. They encountered an issue where multiple items with the same item name but different transaction numbers were affected when deleting or voiding an item. Deleting an item from one transaction also removed the same item from other transactions.', 'The current system did not distinguish items with the same name but different transaction numbers during the delete/void process. A system update was required to ensure that only the selected transaction item would be deleted.', 'Updated the program to correctly identify items based on their transaction number during the delete/void process. Tested the updated system to verify that only the intended item was removed. Backed up the client`s database and file system, then updated the file system on the client`s server.', 'Done'),
(3041, '15123060', '2026-07-03', 'MARK DY', 'ANGELES CITY', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client requested support regarding a transaction where the subtotal and total displayed in the Transaction Vault Review did not match.', 'The transaction was processed using split payment, consisting of â‚±1,500.00 via PayMaya and â‚±447.00 in cash. The Transaction Vault Review only displayed the cash payment, which caused the discrepancy.', 'Accessed the client`s POS system and backed up the database. Reviewed the affected transaction and explained to the client that the Transaction Vault Review only displays the cash portion of split-payment transactions. Advised the client that the complete transaction details, including all payment methods, can be viewed in the Admin ] Sales Invoice Logs/Details.', 'Done');
INSERT INTO `bucket_technotes` (`id`, `accountnum`, `xdate`, `clientname`, `address`, `techname`, `reasonoftech`, `causeoftheissue`, `resso`, `status`) VALUES
(3042, '15724957', '2026-07-06', 'MR OGIE ABESAMIS', 'TALAVERA NUEVA ECIJA', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'Client send the monthly adjustment sales for the month of June 2026', 'Sto Rosario - Monthly sales adjustment Need sales 1,172,975.52 SI No. - 23217\r\nAndal - Monthly sales adjustment Need sales 812,018.47 SI No. - 55655\r\nSibul - Monthly sales adjustment Need sales 791,793.38 SI No. - 24094\r\n', 'Asked the client to open ultraviewer to gain access backed up the database dump itemcount.sql and voiditems.sql and adjusted the sales, after that access executed the updated itemcount.sql and voiditems.sql files to their database.', 'Done'),
(3043, '58449021', '2026-07-06', 'MR OGIE ABESAMIS', 'TALAVERA NUEVA ECIJA', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client reported that the voided items in their Day End Report were being duplicated. They provided photos of the reports for verification.', 'Upon investigation, it was found that when the cashier voids an item and enters the required access code, there is sometimes a slight delay before the system processes the request. During this delay, the cashier may repeatedly press the Enter key, assuming the first input was not registered. As a result, the system records multiple void entries, causing duplicate records to appear in the Day End Report.', 'Accessed the client`s system and created a backup of the database. Simulated the voiding process and successfully reproduced the issue. After confirming the cause, I explained to the client that they should wait for the system to process the access code after pressing Enter and avoid pressing the key multiple times. This will prevent duplicate void entries from being recorded in the report.', 'Done'),
(3044, '10750156', '2026-07-06', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'MADAPDAP MABALACAT', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'Client requested support regarding Terminal 4, as when it was turned on, it did not proceed to the POS system. Upon checking inside the CPU unit, it was observed that the CPU fan was spinning intermittently (turning on and off).', 'Possible loose internal connection affecting system power initialization, resulting in intermittent CPU fan operation.', 'Assisted the client thru call. Powered off the workstation and reseated the 24-pin ATX motherboard power connector, 4-pin CPU power connector, CMOS battery, and RAM modules. Powered on the system and performed testing to verify that the CPU fan is operating normally. Also adjusted the system date to the correct current date and synchronized the date and time settings. After testing, the workstation was confirmed to be stable and functioning properly. The POS system is also working correctly and ', 'Done'),
(3045, '58449021', '2026-07-09', 'MR OGIE ABESAMIS', 'TALAVERA NUEVA ECIJA', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client requested a monthly sales adjustment for the month of June 2026. Additionally, the San Pascual branch reported that they were unable to log in to the POS because the desktop shortcut icon had been accidentally deleted.', 'San Pascual: Monthly sales adjustment required for sales worth 26k with SI No. 30791. The POS shortcut icon was also missing from the desktop, preventing users from launching the system.\r\nSampaloc: Monthly sales adjustment required for sales worth 35k with SI No. 56224.\r\n', 'Connected to both branches through AnyDesk to gain remote access. Before making any changes, backed up the database by exporting the itemcount.sql and voiditems.sql files. Performed the requested monthly sales adjustments, then executed the updated itemcount.sql and voiditems.sql files to apply the changes to the database. Lastly, recreated the deleted POS desktop shortcut in the San Pascual branch to restore access to the system.', 'Done'),
(3046, '60452560', '2026-07-16', 'ANDREWS FOOD MFG', 'BALAGTAS , BULACAN', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client requested an onsite support visit to troubleshoot the system unit in the small office because it was stuck on boot. They also requested us to check the production system unit due to intermittent internet disconnections, which were causing issues with their attendance system.', 'The system unit in the small office had a defective SSD, preventing the operating system from booting properly. For the production system unit, several LAN cables connecting the network devices had poor terminations, resulting in unstable network connectivity.', 'We first diagnosed the system unit in the small office. After performing several troubleshooting procedures, we confirmed that the SSD was defective. We replaced the SSD free of charge, reinstalled the operating system, configured the attendance system, and performed testing to ensure it was functioning properly.\r\n\r\nNext, we checked the production system unit and found that the LAN cables required re-crimping. We re-crimped the network cables to restore stable connectivity.\r\n\r\nTo improve system ', 'Done'),
(3047, '80864793', '2026-07-25', 'TINE SAGMIT', 'BERTHAPHIL CLARK', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client requested onsite support because the POS unexpectedly restarted again. According to the client, this is the second occurrence since the previous support visit.', 'The exact cause of the unexpected restart has not yet been confirmed. Based on the observed symptoms, the Power Supply Unit (PSU) was identified as the most likely cause and was replaced to eliminate the possibility of power-related issues. The client was advised to continue monitoring the system.', 'Arrived at the client`s restaurant and performed a database backup before replacing the existing PSU with a new one. After the replacement, tested the POS to verify that it was operating normally. Advised the client to continue monitoring the system for any recurrence of the issue. Also recommended connecting the UPS directly to a dedicated wall outlet to ensure a stable power supply.\r\n', 'Done'),
(3048, '10750156', '2026-07-28', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'MADAPDAP MABALACAT', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client requested assistance in replacing an existing access code and adding a new access code for their POS system.', 'The client required an updated access code configuration for their POS system.', 'Accessed the client`s POS system and performed a database backup before making any changes. Added the new access code, replaced the required access code, and removed the obsolete access code. Verified that the updated access code configuration was successfully applied and functioning properly.', 'Done'),
(3049, '94506167', '2026-07-28', 'MARLON TOLENTINO', 'CONCEPCION TARLAC', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client requested support because the server thermal printer was not printing, and POS Terminal 3 unexpectedly shut down.', 'A print job became stuck in the printer queue, causing succeeding print jobs to remain pending. The unexpected shutdown of POS Terminal 3 could not be determined during the inspection and requires further monitoring if the issue recurs. A possible factor may be an unstable power supply or power connection.', 'Accessed the server and cleared the pending print jobs in the printer queue, restoring normal printing operations. Checked the power connection of POS Terminal 3 and connected the system unit directly to a dedicated wall outlet to eliminate the possibility of an unstable UPS power supply. Advised the client to continue monitoring the terminal for any recurrence of the issue.', 'Done'),
(3050, '94506167', '2026-07-29', 'MARLON TOLENTINO', 'CONCEPCION TARLAC', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'The client requested the creation of a return process in their warehousing system and requested that the category list be arranged in alphabetical order.', 'The current warehousing system did not have a return process feature, and the category list was not sorted alphabetically, making navigation and item selection less efficient.', 'The programmer updated the warehousing system by adding the requested return process feature and modifying the category list to display in alphabetical order. After completing the development and testing, accessed the client`s warehouse system remotely, deployed the updates, and demonstrated the new features to the client through a remote session and phone call.', 'Done'),
(3051, '39536570', '2026-07-29', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'BAKELKEL MADAPDAP', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'Client want to update their products in bakelkel', 'Outdated price of products of bakelkel', 'Get the updated products in buddys server then access the POS of bakelkel and render it the updated products.', 'Done'),
(3052, '39536570', '2026-07-30', 'JACQUELYN GALANG', 'BAKELKEL MADAPDAP', 'CHRISTIAN BUNGQUE', 'Client want to update their products in bakelkel', 'Outdated price of products of bakelkel', 'Get the updated products in buddys server then access the POS of bakelkel and render it the updated products.', 'Done');
